[Music]  in celebration of the unlikely  adventurer who started jrr tolkien's  epic lord of the rings adventure  this is the bilbo baggin story explained  bilbo baggins was born in the shire in  the year 2890 of the third age  the only son of bungo baggins in  belladonna took  bilbo spent his early life in the hobbit  hole known as bagant  which would remain his family home after  the death of his parents  as a boy bilbo always wanted to know  more about the things that were  happening outside the shire  this unusual trait drew the attention of  the wizard gandalf  but as bilbo got older he seemed to lose  this quality  he lived alone and was pleased to enjoy  the same comforts as his fellow hobbits  food drink and leisure and never causing  trouble for his neighbors  though bilbo didn't know it that was set  to change after he turned 50.  bilbo's early adulthood passed in quiet  comforted back end  but his calm life was disrupted by the  arrival of gandalf  who asked bilbo to take part in an  upcoming quest  soon strange dwarves began arriving on  bilbo's doorstep  13 in all the dwarves were led by thorin  oakenshield who explained to bilbo that  they were on their way  to erebor to reclaim their ancestral  home in the lonely mountain  the dragon smaug had forced the dwarves  out years earlier and now rested there  hoarding the treasure inside which is  why the dwarves needed bilbo's help  that's why we need a burglar good one  too  an expert i'd imagine and are you  bilbo was reluctant to go since he  didn't consider himself a burglar at all  but he ultimately agreed to set out from  the shire with the  on an dwarves after venturing out with  doran and company  bilbo encountered a trio of trolls who  nearly put an  end to the quest before gandalf came to  the rescue when the trolls turned to  stone  bilbo and the dwarves were able to raid  their nearby cave  it was here that bilbo discovered his  sword sting which he would keep for many  years  the company eventually reached the elven  city of rivendell  where bilbo met elrond for the first  time bilbo developed a fascination with  the elves  which he would carry with him for the  rest of his life the company left  rivendell to pass through the misty  mountains where they tried to shelter in  a cave  they soon found the goblins were  infesting the mountain and while bilbo  managed to escape  capture thorin and company were not so  lucky while the dwarves and gandalf  dealt with the goblins bilbo stumbled  through the dark and happened to find a  golden ring  soon after he encountered a strange  creature known as gollum  who threatened to eat him unless he  could win a riddle contest  bilbo stumped gollum with his final  riddle  what have i got in my pocket  as gollum grew more frustrated bilbo put  the ring on and vanished  gollum thought the hobbit had found a  way out and gave chase toward the cave  exit  bilbo used his newfound invisibility to  follow gollum making his way out of the  cave  outside bilbo reunited with the dwarves  who'd managed to fight their way out of  the misty mountains  the group was then attacked by wargs  only to be rescued by gandalf's friends  the great eagles  when the company finally arrived at the  lonely mountain bilbo snuck in through  the secret door on thorin's map  bilbo's entrance woke the dragon smaug  so bilbo put on the ring to stay hidden  and kept smaug busy with riddles until  he discovered the dragon had a bare  patch in his armor  bilbo told the dwarves of smaug's  weakness and a nearby thrush heard and  told  bard the bowman of nearby laketown when  smaug flew into a rage  and departed the mountain to burn the  town in retribution for bilbo's thievery  bard shot the dragon in the bare spot  killing him  but the struggle with the dragon was  only the beginning of the battle  groups of men and elves soon arrived to  lay claim to the mountain's treasure  the dwarves sent word to their own kind  for help  and just as a battle was about to ensue  bilbo revealed that he'd stolen the  arkanstone  the dwarf's most prized artifact from  the mountain  bilbo used it to try to broker peace but  soon  all three factions were interrupted by a  goblin army in the ensuing battle  known as the battle of five armies due  to the eagle's eventual participation  thorin was killed putting an end to his  quest to reclaim his kingdom  bilbo was supposed to receive 1 14th of  the lonely mountain's treasure but  instead  settled for two chests of gold and  silver he returned home to the shire  and when he arrived at bag end he  discovered that there was another battle  to fight  you're not supposed to be here what do  you mean  on account of you being presumed dead  enough  i am not dead presumed  is jealous and meddling cousins the  sackville baggins  had begun to auction off all of his  belongings so they could move into  baghdad themselves  only after buying back every piece of  his own furniture himself could bilbo  settle back into a normal life  he eventually began a book recounting  his adventures titled  there and back again but bilbo would  never be the same again  his long journey and surprising return  had led to rumors and whispers about  what he'd done  and what he was up to all alone in bag  end more importantly though he didn't  know it at the time  the ring he'd discovered in the misty  mountains had begun to take hold of him  as a result bilbo hardly seemed to age  at all for the next 60 years  as bilbo's 111th birthday celebration  approached  bilbo decided to head off on one final  adventure before his death  i want to see mountains again mountains  gandalf  bilbo's birthday party was massive and  bilbo ended it by putting on the ring  and disappearing  after the party bilbo prepared to set  out for rivendell  but gandalf confronted him about the  rings aware of the effect it was having  on his old friend  the wizard urged bilbo to leave the ring  along with bag end to his nephew frodo  bilbo was initially resistant but after  he calmed down he realized the wisdom of  gandalf's advice  bilbo gave the ring up and left the  shire unbeknownst to bilbo  gandalf's research would soon confirm  that the ring was in fact  the one ring forged by the dark lord  sauron  in a bid to control all of middle earth  by letting it go  and leaving it to frodo bilbo became the  first individual in the ring's history  to relinquish it voluntarily  bilbo stayed in the realm of elrond for  some time then left again to visit the  city of dale and gaze upon the lonely  mountain one more time  before returning again to rivendell  there he continued to work on his book  and began to notice that age was  catching up to him without the ring  he grew weaker and more feeble  eventually frodo arrived in rivendell  with the ring on a quest to destroy it  bilbo  still harbored a desire for the ring but  knew it was best if frodo succeeded in  his quest  bilbo gifted his nephew with two  remaining artifacts from his adventures  his sword sting and a mithril shirt  while bilbo remained in rivendell frodo  kept pushing toward mordor  eventually frodo succeeded in destroying  the ring  ushering in the fourth age the fourth  age came to be known as the age of men  since the great elven leaders left the  continent to sail west to the undying  lands  because they had been ring bearers frodo  and bilbo were invited to accompany  elrond  and the lady galadriel of lothlorien  across the sea  before departing middle earth bilbo  turned 131  making him the oldest hobbit in the  continent's history  he sailed west and presumably passed  away  in the undying lands at peace check out  one of our newest videos right here  plus even more looper videos about the  lord of the rings are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one

